        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(feishu): lock timeoutMs preflight abort for stalled DNS lookup",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFeishu app registration can hang indefinitely when SSRF preflight DNS/proxy lookup never completes. Without a regression at the `beginAppRegistration` entry point, a future change can lose guard-owned `timeoutMs` abort and again leave onboarding stuck before HTTP dispatch.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nCurrent `main` already owns timeouts via `fetchWithSsrFGuard` top-level `timeoutMs` (not `AbortSignal.timeout()`). This PR is test-only: it locks that contract for a never-resolving `lookupFn`, asserting the same guard diagnostic already covered for hang-without-headers (`TimeoutError` + `message: \"request timed out\"`) and that `fetchImpl` is never called.\n\nRebuilt onto latest `main` (`edef9822eefc0cef68b2c7b2e965a2daf32341d9`) per ClawSweeper rebase guidance.\n\nAI-assisted: yes. I inspected current `beginAppRegistration` / `fetchFeishuJson`, sibling hang-without-headers coverage, and the guard timeout diagnostic before updating the regression.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo runtime change. Contributors and CI keep a focused lock that stalled Feishu registration preflight fails closed with the guard-owned timeout diagnostic and without opening an HTTP request.\n\n## Evidence\n\n| Layer | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| L1 | `pnpm exec vitest run extensions/feishu/src/app-registration.test.ts -t \"preflight lookup stalls\\|never return headers\"` → **2 passed** |\n| Stall proof | `timed_out=true name=TimeoutError message=request timed out elapsed_ms=81 fetch_called=0` |\n| Scope | 1 file / +35 −0 vs `main` `edef982…`; tip `dd2a6136254c50a67bf66126b7dafd6eb1dd9715` |\n\n```text\n[feishu preflight stall proof] timed_out=true name=TimeoutError message=request timed out elapsed_ms=81 fetch_called=0\n```\n",
